# `t:trans6`, on a supplied **physical Satin** trajectory and sector

User-facing file. Namespace `VacuumSelection.Spine` for the `TransSix` statement.

* Physics accounts: Lean `Ledger.lean`, `Channel.lean`, `Tapestry` and `P.ElectedChart`:
  input P is a `Spine`, not a field-law placeholder. In the coordinates of the paper the
  level-zero **matter** spacing is one. For normalization & qualification on the original finite
  `Pay` bills (in code comments we also say Pe or PE for such finite period/cutoff
  enquiries, `Journey.compass`, `sharp`, `taking` etc.)
  use `account_pe`, `coupling_confirmed`; sources `st_price`, `source_bill`, `color_identity`,
  `ap_slots`. For sector use in the result see `axis_prescription`, `pane`,
  `Arrivals.lean`. Especially: `P.sixBody s n j` (j : Window.Family). `S, F, Between`, widths are
  exactly of `the construction notes`; body opposition `kiss` uses `Spine.reflectTest`. For budgets use
  `occupiedSpace`. `P.frameLight_limit`, `Decimal.lean: P.positions_footprint`,
  `mayPlace`, `Forever`, `Consult`. `Realized` each proves the answer from the actual signed
  purchases, including identification by the **SAME** character on each native high label
  (and even identically the `spirits` polynomial answer), both pose locations charged with
  widths, stencils at every refinement, both densities independently integrated
  (`P.measureField` and `P.measureAt`; `P.consult_limit`). `detectorSelect` and
  `P.PricePaid.detector` supplemental prove that these paid purchases can additionally
  be authorized through existence of a selector, on a specified ratio recipe on the actual microscopic reading, in terms of the
  one SU(5) gauge field U with coupled Sea on those trajectory marks and indeed still at
  physical location (not asking the finite ratio at variable t before these selections).
  See also `Authorize.lean` `Realized.contour`. Period/cutoff/height order important. NO identification of single-label unselected
  Pe limit with the `singleState` price; that limit would be to the ensemble mean.
  See accompanying proof directory; these theorems use the exact supplied starting API's
  `P` conventions.
* Hypotheses `P`, `R`, `x` at axis 3, `Chosen` from the `Prototype.summit`
  purchases (we collect `Launch`, `readyUV`, `LowerDeck`,
  `Summit`, `party` on those data, including the `P.Ellis 3 x` in the inputs). Probe resolutions depend on
  this choice. If additionally starting from `uniform` P (which can even retain all
  `RibbonCourse` conditions with `Prepared` etc via `supplied`), witness x thence
  available with all these ingredients (`Spine.onSupplied`, `Spine.RibbonCourse.once`).
  Can use `transSix` itself for all the x's already in `Prototype.summit`'s output; its
  other conclusions may thus be kept too. No changes of Hilbert representation, coupling
  or history—in particular we ARE using `P.history`, `P.Register` (
  value `R`) which identifies these SAME cost transfers. For changing **axes in the analytic
  estimates**, strictly use the prescribed common-character price on all the axes. Not
  applying prices from any other history. `Spine.same_spectrum`
  shows `P.otherSpectrum i i x=x`, as we often keep `x₃` in `ManyF 3` etc to truly be
  `P.otherSpectrum 3 3 x` (same usage as `Prototype`/`Bands`).
* Output includes exact Zoom and purchases, including hypotheses fit for both Part(i),(ii).
  Presets: may first use arbitrary positive radii ball in the stated cone with octant
  qualification (we allow more: `SpectralWindow`). There are always such balls of the
  stated kind too (`Spine.always_windows`). May pre-specify any center rectangles with
  margins in the closure sense of `RectanglePose.Across`, or using `Settle.rectangles` first
  fix the measurement i then choose ANY rectangles of center poses that still fit
  the paying gaps *including the field footprints* there. In addition to those
  prices for centers (including approximation in any C^k test cost there), can keep
  the whole footprints *inside* the given rectangles by choosing insets (pre-specify
  the rectangles first for this). None of these choose shrinking-radius labels at the
  RHS limit of our realized purchases: fix `(s,n)` (i.e. `(c i,r i)`) fields and fix pose budget,
  fix the smearing tests (may even use ones selected arbitrarily close to pre-specified
  mac tests there, not concentrated around some point), then grants on the finer and finer t,
  through t -> ∞. Matrix positive price in Part(i) is entirely from positive time energy
  and even after projecting the vectors to `press ...` of the pre-specified region. This bound may, of
  course, depend on `i,f`; no assertion of uniform signal in the further UV limit i→∞
  after physically separated placements. Part(ii) asks instead for a decisive absolute
  discrepancy on THIS DISTANT measurement; it needn't be Hermitian at all. Stability on
  perturbing supports/smears independently through L¹ with qualification (`Through`) in
  `Realized.perturb`, `Forever.perturb_floor`. See also
  `Realized.slackFloor` for the version with two eventualities (also in observation t),
  `Questions.openCenters` for explicit independent movements of the centers, and
  `Achieves.stillPaints`. Density of the rectangle-rank grants among tests
  in any predetermined C^k cost follows
  from `RectangleAward`. All inputs and perturbations here are in the **smooth real test
  density questions** with the stated frame; not a statement about smoothing arbitrarily
  posed overlapping physical observables. Opposite-sign poses in Part(ii) naturally
  available; choose any strict axis orientations on the three transverse axes.
* Test against factoring between RAW paired-link gauge stencil and even chiral matter.
  Height of the marginal is the queried `t`. Accept any such normalized prediction with
  Ward on at least one of those algebras (`Pockets.Comparison`), `PaintedSplit` even weaker.
  All such give zero. In particular the very split formed by restricting M on each is
  disqualified, for both kinds of tests. No pricing of dressed-variable predictors with
  purported independence without computing these source contractions. `Report.lean` and
  `AuditPocket.lean` verify the endpoint-pocket center-charge obstruction at every height.

NOT a claim of relativistic construction of chiral SU(5), still Euclidean and still on the
strictly order-budgeted placements. The kernel can use real space & real EUCLIDEAN time
of these labels. No claim spacelike field locality—in particular do not apply these proofs
in place of a `Fern.OnOrion.spacelikeWidthWitness` question, on a different apparatus.
Not deriving a width failure on *this* sector from that other apparatus either. Left-handed
is the precise bare chiral identification of the operators/system (all 3 generations,
`wedge2 ⊕ overbar-f`, project signs/Spin, prescribed projection), not an assertion of
relativistic symmetry or a claim that the entire joint spectrum is in the
forward Minkowski cone. For the `Launch`-dependent part of the proof we adapt,
in particular, the `Cordial` estimates onto the mixed entries. In particular don't use any
fixed-stencil UV price as if it were uniform on these moving tests; use of an earlier
Wick capacity for the move has all its hypotheses verified in `MixedUV`/`ProjectedUV`.
-/
